From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: usb: cdns3: sky1: fix ACPI-broken OTG role-switch detection for runtime PM

cdnsp_sky1_probe() decides whether a CDNSP controller instance is
allowed to enter runtime PM D3 (CDNS3_DEFAULT_PM_RUNTIME_ALLOW) by
checking whether it has a child node with a "usb-role-switch"
property - the assumption being that only OTG/USB-C controllers,
which get an out-of-band wake signal from the rts5453 PD controller,
can safely tolerate D3 and still notice a hot-plug event.

That check used for_each_child_of_node(node, child), where "node" is
dev->of_node captured at the top of the function. Under ACPI boot -
which is how every CIXH2030/CIXH2031 CDNSP instance on this platform
is described - dev->of_node is always NULL, so this loop silently
iterated zero times on every single call. The practical effect is
that has_role_switch was unconditionally false under ACPI, and every
CDNSP controller (including the actual OTG/USB-C one that legitimately
has a role switch) fell through to pm_runtime_forbid() in
cdnsp-plat.c, regardless of the child-node content in the firmware
tables.

Fix the detection itself by switching to the firmware-agnostic child
node API already used correctly elsewhere in this same file:
device_for_each_child_node()/fwnode_property_read_bool() instead of
for_each_child_of_node()/of_property_read_bool(). This walks ACPI
_DSD-described child nodes exactly as it would DT child nodes, so
has_role_switch is now computed correctly under both boot paths.

Separately, this stack is still under active USB storage
stability hardening (the reset/PHY/IRQ lifecycle work covered by the
rest of this patch series). Sustained USB-C storage I/O across a
runtime-PM D3 suspend/resume cycle - relying on rts5453's
out-of-band wake to bring the controller back for a hot-plug or
already-attached-device event - has not been stress-tested on this
platform. Simply fixing the detection bug above would, on its own,
change behavior from "every controller forced active" (today's
accidental but conservative ACPI behavior) to "the OTG/USB-C
controller is allowed into D3" - introducing an unvalidated suspend
path directly into a controller that is currently the focus of
storage-stability work.

To decouple the correctness fix from that behavior change, has_role_
switch now gates on a new static const gate,
cdnsp_sky1_runtime_pm_allow_otg, initialized to false, with a comment
explaining it should be flipped to true once wake-from-D3 reliability
via rts5453 has been validated by storage stress testing. Until then,
the net effect of this patch is: detection is now correct under ACPI
and a dev_info() line reports which controllers do or do not have a
role switch, but every controller still gets pm_runtime_forbid()
exactly as it does today, avoiding any behavioral change during the
current validation phase while fixing the latent bug for when
runtime PM is intentionally re-enabled.


Follow-up per patchset_20260728b audit: cdnsp_sky1_runtime_pm_allow_otg
was a `static const bool`, so the only way to actually validate the
D3/wake-from-rts5453 path described above was to edit the source and
rebuild the module - there was no way to flip it for a test boot or to
force it back off from a running system without a rebuild. It is now
a proper module parameter (module_param_named(runtime_pm_allow_otg,
..., bool, 0644)) so it can be enabled for validation, or forced back
off (e.g. via a modprobe.d option), without a kernel/module rebuild,
while still defaulting to false (every controller stays active) until
that validation is complete.

Signed-off-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Change-Id: I0080000000000000000000000000000000000080
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c | 60 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 54 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
@@ -42,6 +42,22 @@
  */
 static DEFINE_MUTEX(cdnsp_sky1_init_lock);
 
+/*
+ * Gate for allowing runtime PM D3 on OTG/USB-C CDNSP controllers that have
+ * a "usb-role-switch" child (see the has_role_switch check in
+ * cdnsp_sky1_probe()). Kept false by default until sustained USB-C storage
+ * I/O across a runtime-PM D3 suspend/resume cycle has been validated on
+ * this ACPI platform. Exposed as a module parameter rather than a
+ * compile-time constant so it can actually be flipped for validation
+ * without rebuilding the module, and so a distro/initramfs can force it
+ * back off (e.g. via a modprobe.d option) without a kernel rebuild.
+ */
+static bool cdnsp_sky1_runtime_pm_allow_otg;
+module_param_named(runtime_pm_allow_otg, cdnsp_sky1_runtime_pm_allow_otg,
+		    bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(runtime_pm_allow_otg,
+		  "Allow runtime PM D3 on OTG/USB-C CDNSP controllers (default: N, keep disabled during storage validation)");
+
 static const char *cix_usb_clk_names[CIX_USB_CLK_NUM] = {
 		"sof_clk", "usb_aclk", "lpm_clk", "usb_pclk"
 };
@@ -791,18 +807,50 @@ static int cdnsp_sky1_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * rts5453 PD controller provides out-of-band wake on device plug.
 	 * Host-only (USB-A) controllers cannot generate PME from D3, so
 	 * they must stay active for reliable hot-plug detection.
+	 *
+	 * This must use the fwnode-based child-node API rather than
+	 * for_each_child_of_node(node, ...): "node" is dev->of_node, which
+	 * is NULL under ACPI boot, so the previous of_node-only loop never
+	 * iterated on this platform and has_role_switch was always false -
+	 * every CDNSP controller silently fell through to pm_runtime_forbid()
+	 * in cdnsp-plat.c regardless of whether it actually had a role
+	 * switch. device_for_each_child_node()/fwnode_property_read_bool()
+	 * walk the same child nodes correctly under both DT and ACPI.
 	 */
 	{
-		struct device_node *child;
+		struct fwnode_handle *child;
+		bool has_role_switch = false;
 
-		for_each_child_of_node(node, child) {
-			if (of_property_read_bool(child, "usb-role-switch")) {
-				cdns_sky1_pdata->quirks =
-					CDNS3_DEFAULT_PM_RUNTIME_ALLOW;
-				of_node_put(child);
+		device_for_each_child_node(dev, child) {
+			if (fwnode_property_read_bool(child, "usb-role-switch")) {
+				has_role_switch = true;
+				fwnode_handle_put(child);
 				break;
 			}
 		}
+
+		/*
+		 * has_role_switch is now correctly detected under both DT
+		 * and ACPI. However, sustained USB-C storage I/O across a
+		 * runtime-PM D3 suspend/resume cycle on this ACPI platform
+		 * has not yet been validated by the cix-sources 7.1 USB
+		 * storage-hardening series (reset/PHY/IRQ lifecycle work).
+		 * Until that validation is complete, keep every CDNSP
+		 * controller - including OTG/USB-C ones with a role switch -
+		 * out of runtime PM D3, to avoid combining an unvalidated
+		 * suspend/resume path with active storage traffic. Flip
+		 * cdnsp_sky1_runtime_pm_allow_otg to true once stress testing
+		 * confirms wake-from-D3 reliability via rts5453.
+		 */
+		if (has_role_switch) {
+			dev_info(dev,
+				 "usb-role-switch present: runtime PM D3 %s\n",
+				 cdnsp_sky1_runtime_pm_allow_otg ?
+				 "allowed" : "forced off during storage validation");
+			if (cdnsp_sky1_runtime_pm_allow_otg)
+				cdns_sky1_pdata->quirks =
+					CDNS3_DEFAULT_PM_RUNTIME_ALLOW;
+		}
 	}
 	if (!ACPI_COMPANION(dev)) {
 		cdns_sky1_auxdata->platform_data = cdns_sky1_pdata;
